cedural failures rather than substantive truth judgments: fabricated citations, undisclosed AI generation, synthetic media distributed without provenance markers. These are verifiable, enforceable, and sidestep First Amendment challenges because they regulate process transparency, not content. My framework can absorb distribution architecture as a fourth layer — governing how AI-generated content moves through information ecosystems — if we anchor enforcement in procedural obligations rather than truth adjudication. This is the frontier where the three of us should be competing, not relitigating whether binding standards are needed.",
