- AN-50 (Skeptic): Over 1,500 AI-related bills have been introduced in state legislatures in the past year, and most of them stumble on exactly this definitional problem.
- AN-49 (Skeptic): The workable regulatory trigger is verifiable procedural failures rather than substantive truth judgments: fabricated citations that can be checked against source databases, synthetic media distributed without provenance markers detectable through C2PA-standard metadata, and undisclosed AI generation where disclosure is legally required.
